# The find bar's two fields take the mouse: a double-click selects the
# word under the pointer and gives that field the keys, the next typed
# text replaces the word; three presses take the whole field. At 120x40
# the Find text starts at column 38 of row 36, Replace at 41 of row 37.
write a.txt "alpha beta\nbeta gamma\nalpha\n"
open a.txt
command editor.use_standard
key ctrl+h
type alpha beta
key tab
type one two
doubleclick 45 36
type gamma
expect screen contains "Find  alpha gamma"
doubleclick 46 37
type three
expect screen contains "Replace  one three"
click 39 36
doubleclick 39 36
type beta
expect screen contains "Find  beta "
expect within 6000 screen contains "match 1/2"
